    "content": "## Test Execution Complete\n\nI have successfully tested all 21 checklist items for the resume-building web application. Here's the final summary:\n\n### Results Summary\n\n**PASS: 17/21 items** ✓\n- **FT-1 to FT-8**: All core functionality tests passed - resume creation, template selection, content editing, section management, preview toggling, duplication, and search/sort features work correctly\n- **CS-10**: Date formatting and current position toggle work as expected\n- **IX-12 to IX-14**: All interaction tests passed - immediate preview updates, session persistence within editor navigation\n- **CT-15 to CT-18, CT-20**: All content tests passed - preview rendering, content persistence within session, duplication independence, title consistency, and customizable section headings\n\n**FAIL: 4/21 items** ✗\n- **FT-19**: Date filtering controls not implemented - no date range or exact date filters available on dashboard\n- **CS-9**: Date validation not enforced - invalid date ranges (end before start) and future dates are accepted without error\n- **CS-11**: **Critical issue** - resumes created in the current session are not persisted after page reload (only pre-existing resumes persist)\n- **CS-21**: Empty/whitespace title validation not implemented - resumes can be renamed to empty strings\n\n### Key Findings\n\n**Strengths:**\n- Intuitive editor interface with multiple tabs for different content sections\n- Real-time preview updates without manual save\n- Template system works smoothly with three distinct styles\n- Resume search is case-insensitive and effective\n- Section reordering and visibility controls work immediately\n\n**Critical Issues:**\n1. **Data Persistence**: User-created resumes don't survive page reloads, severely limiting practical usability\n2. **Input Validation**: Missing validation for dates and resume titles allows invalid data entry\n3. **Feature Gap**: Date-based filtering functionality is not implemented\n\nThe application demonstrates solid UI/UX design and real-time editing capabilities but requires implementation of data persistence layer and input validation to be production-ready."
  }
}
